{
	"name": "ModeHud",
	"_doc": "The game modes' top bar (src/client/ModeHud; Rules/ModeHud, Config/ModeHud; user 2026-10-29, option B of the mode HUD drafts, the front bar: \"use the basic font ... remove the capturing bar completely. just make the diamond on the top show the progress\"). FrontBar, Territory Push (src/server/Frontline): the two nations at the ends (flag and name; the viewer's side always on the left), a bar filled with each side's team rim colour from its end to the front (the share of the chain it holds, the fought-over sector's control counting), a white tick at the front, and one diamond per sector on the bar (Pin, PinHQ for the HQs: the code clones them per sector, evenly spaced, with a PinLabel under each). A diamond fills from its bottom tip in the colour of the side its control leans to, as far as the control goes (the flag's height on the pole); its edge turns pinContested on even numbers in the zone, pinAttacked when its holder is outnumbered there. Result: the winner during the results. ZoneBar, Point Capture (FFA, src/server/ZoneMatch; user 2026-10-29: \"center the timer and remove the bar completely\"): the match clock centred, the point leader under it (\"remove the top score and your score. just keep track of the score leader and display it\"; the leader's glow is the server's), the zone's state, then the move warning. No panels. Sizes in reference pixels at theme.scale.referenceHeight, one UIScale. Colours: Config/Palette UI.Hud names. One font, the game's basic font. Desktop only.",
